      "worked": "Write $a=kbc$. Using the first data column:\n$$\\begin{align*}12&=k\\times1\\times1\\\\k&=12\\\\a&=12bc\\end{align*}$$\nFor the second column:\n$$\\begin{align*}24&=12\\times b\\times2\\\\b&=1\\end{align*}$$\nFor the third column:\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=12\\times2\\times1\\\\a&=24\\end{align*}$$\nFor the fourth column:\n$$\\begin{align*}48&=12\\times b\\times2\\\\b&=2\\end{align*}$$\nFor the fifth column:\n$$\\begin{align*}72&=12\\times2\\times c\\\\c&=3\\end{align*}$$",
